1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,900
Not here either.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,000
Tom Thomas, are you looking for me? Huh?

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,500
No, for a red pen. I need it right now.

4
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,800
What do you need it for?

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,400
Here, look what my teacher wrote in my assignment book.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:28,400
Bad behavior during the lesson, fidgeting, and talking.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:29,900
What are you going to do with the red pen?

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,560
pen. Your teacher left something out. I thought maybe, you know, I could fix it a bit. I hope I

9
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,500
find that pen.

10
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,500
Oh, what?

11
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:48,000
What?

12
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,240
Oh wow! Good catch!

13
00:00:55,039 --> 00:00:58,719
So, what do you want to fix on it? I'll just add a couple of no's,

14
00:00:58,719 --> 00:01:03,079
And then it will say that I had no bad behavior during the lesson,

15
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:05,239
no fidgeting, and no talking.

16
00:01:05,359 --> 00:01:06,439
See? No problem!

17
00:01:06,439 --> 00:01:07,239
Cool!

18
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:09,039
And then add this at the end.

19
00:01:09,159 --> 00:01:11,239
Tom Thomas is a perfect student!

20
00:01:12,319 --> 00:01:14,640
Nah, then they would guess I did it.

21
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:17,759
What, is it clogged up?

22
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:19,439
A little scribble will do it.

23
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:25,280
That's not a pen. It's more like a penknife.

24
00:01:26,519 --> 00:01:28,680
Oh, look! The ball is missing!

25
00:01:28,719 --> 00:01:30,439
What ball? It's a pen!

26
00:01:30,519 --> 00:01:31,560
It's a pen!

27
00:01:31,679 --> 00:01:33,480
But it's a ballpoint pen!

28
00:01:35,679 --> 00:01:39,680
Old-fashioned pens work by dipping the pen into a jar of ink.

29
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,840
But with a ballpoint pen,

30
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:46,799
the ink is stored inside of a tube that has a metal tip on the end with a small steel ball.

31
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:51,439
Well, small for humans, that is, but of course for Fixies it's quite large.

32
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,960
When you drag the pen across the paper,

33
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:57,480
the ball spins around and gets ink on it from inside the tube.

34
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:01,160
Then it turns over and the ink rolls out onto the paper.

35
00:02:01,439 --> 00:02:04,880
So without the ball, a ballpoint pen won't write at all.

36
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,159
So what am I going to do? That's my only red pen.

37
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,199
Hi everybody!

38
00:02:18,319 --> 00:02:19,719
Why do you look so sad?

39
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:23,040
Uh, we lost the ball from the tip of this pen. Where?

40
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,240
It's here somewhere.

41
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,879
Then you're in luck, boys!

42
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:28,479
In the pack-o-mat, there's a metal detector.

43
00:02:28,599 --> 00:02:31,479
You can use it to find different kinds of metal objects.

44
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,759
No, that's not it.

45
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,079
I can see that myself.

46
00:02:45,159 --> 00:02:46,879
It's not on the table, Nolik.

47
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:51,960
Until not that long ago,

48
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:57,280
humans used pens that had to be dipped over and over again into an inkwell.

49
00:02:57,439 --> 00:02:59,360
This was quite inconvenient,

50
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:03,360
and so to make writing easier, the fountain pen was invented.

51
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,960
A fountain pen could be filled up with ink,

52
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,800
so it could write for a much longer time.

53
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:13,400
But fountain pens would often leak, leaving blots of ink on the paper.

54
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:17,840
This problem was solved with the invention of the ballpoint pen.

55
00:03:18,319 --> 00:03:21,520
Ballpoint pens are simple, handy, and reliable,

56
00:03:21,520 --> 00:03:26,520
except that you can't write with them on a wall or upside down for a long time.

57
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:29,520
That's because the ball uses up the ink on it,

58
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:32,320
and the ink can't flow up to the tip.

59
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:34,920
But even this problem has been solved.

60
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:40,920
There are now special ballpoint pens that can be used by astronauts floating in space.

61
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,520
Is this the one?

62
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,000
You're right! That's it!

63
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:58,500
Don't you just see how awesome my metal detector is?

64
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:01,500
Is that what you're calling me now?

65
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Yeah!

66
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,519
Tom Thomas, help us!

67
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,519
And now!

68
00:04:22,519 --> 00:04:23,519
Tideesh!

69
00:04:23,519 --> 00:04:24,120
Cool!

70
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,519
By the way, what do you need the red pen for?

71
00:04:26,519 --> 00:04:30,120
Well, Tom Thomas and I need to fix something in his assignment book.

72
00:04:30,120 --> 00:04:31,120
What?!

73
00:04:31,519 --> 00:04:34,120
If I knew that, I wouldn't have helped you out!

74
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:38,519
So, no fidgeting and no talking. Hmm.

75
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:44,319
And your teacher, she writes in your assignment book when you behave well?

76
00:04:44,319 --> 00:04:45,120
Uh-huh.

77
00:04:45,120 --> 00:04:49,040
Whenever we behave well, she writes a note in our books right away.

78
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:54,840
Ah! Did you see, Simka, how Tom Thomas managed to outsmart everybody?

79
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:57,800
Since I see nothing else here from your teacher,

80
00:04:57,879 --> 00:05:00,120
does that mean you behaved badly the other days?

81
00:05:00,199 --> 00:05:00,959
Uh-huh.

82
00:05:01,319 --> 00:05:01,920
What?!

83
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,399
Well…

84
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:08,079
Did you see, Nolik, how Tom Thomas just managed to outsmart himself?

